<title>USA: Comdisco files shelf for $950 mln debt.</title>
<headline>Comdisco files shelf for $950 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comdisco Inc on Friday filed a shelf registration statement with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $950 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>The filing includes $100 million of previously registered debt securities, said the Rosemont, Ill.,-based buyer, seller and leasor of computers and other high technology equipment.</p>
<p>The company said it will use net proceeds for general corporate purposes, including equipment purchases, repayment of short-term debt and redemption or repurchase of senior debt.</p>
</text>
